## What each account holds

Every account is filled from the same demo data pack. Dates are counted from the day the account was opened or last reset, so the data always looks current. The bookkeeping quarter is the exception: it is always July to September 2026, because the documents are PDFs with printed dates.

**The firm.** Larkspur Corporate Services Pte. Ltd., a corporate services firm in Singapore, with three departments (Secretary, Accounting and Sales), the six people above, three more staff without a sign-in, and a catalogue of fifteen services in SGD.

**The clients.** Twelve fictional companies, each with a part in the demo:

| Client | Part in the demo |
|---|---|
| Kestrel Bay Analytics Pte. Ltd. | Incorporation waiting for ACRA registration. See [Incorporation](/en/demo/incorporation/). |
| Fernreach Botanicals Pte. Ltd. | Incorporation just opened, for ID recognition. |
| Marigold Lane Kitchen Pte. Ltd. | Company C: one-click fill (in preparation); change of registered address; the client checklist; Rachel Lau's portal. |
| Tidewater Studio Pte. Ltd. | Company A: a quarter already booked (in preparation). Also sends InvoiceNow invoices to Marigold Lane. |
| Juniper Forge Engineering Pte. Ltd. | Company B: a quarter half booked (in preparation); change of director. |
| Orchid Mesa Design Pte. Ltd. | Annual return waiting for ACRA filing. |
| Pebblestone Learning Pte. Ltd. | Change of company name. |
| Saffron Quay Trading Pte. Ltd. | Annual return overdue; the case is collecting information. |
| Halcyon Ridge Holdings Pte. Ltd. | Group parent; annual return due in 7 days. |
| Halcyon Ridge Logistics Pte. Ltd. | Subsidiary; share transfer to the parent. |
| Halcyon Ridge Properties Pte. Ltd. | Subsidiary; annual return with AGM documents out for signature. |
| Bramblewood Consulting Pte. Ltd. | Striking off. |

The account also holds opportunities in each stage, invoices in each status, two contract drafts on agreed opportunities, two past AI conversations and two knowledge documents.

## How the demo environment differs from the live service

| Area | In the demo environment |
|---|---|
| Data | Only fictional data. Do not upload real documents or personal data. |
| Email | No email leaves the demo environment. Every email that would be sent (portal sign-in codes, e-sign invitations, invoices) goes to the **Demo inbox** of the account. Only the tenant admin can open it: select the avatar at the bottom of the side bar, then **Demo inbox**. |
| ACRA | The ACRA button opens a mock ACRA website, not Bizfile. The demo version of the ACRA extension fills it. Only annual returns and incorporations have mock pages. For other flows the button cannot be selected, and Operon shows **The demo environment does not provide ACRA filing for this flow.** |
| InvoiceNow | Client companies can send and receive InvoiceNow invoices through a mock Access Point. Nothing reaches the Peppol network. The firm's own InvoiceNow connection is not available. |
| Xero, Stripe | Not connected. Operon shows **Not connected. This integration is not available in the demo environment.** |
| AI conversations | Real AI model calls, limited to USD 1 for each account between resets. See below. |
| Bookkeeping and document reading | Recorded answers are played back. No AI model is called. See [Bookkeeping](/en/demo/bookkeeping/). |
| Filings | Nothing is filed with ACRA or IRAS, and no real e-invoice is sent. |

{% screenshot id="demo/demo-inbox-list" caption="The Demo inbox of an experience account." /%}

## AI conversations: USD 1 for each account

Conversations with the AI employees and with the bookkeeping agent call a real AI model. Each experience account can spend USD 1 on them, counted from the day it was opened or last reset. When the allowance is used up, the conversation shows **This demo's AI allowance is used up. Reset the account to restore it.**

Everything else that uses AI in the demo, such as reading documents, ID recognition and one-click fill, plays back recorded answers and costs nothing. Those features give a result only for the demo documents of the data pack.

## Demo files

Some steps of the demo upload a file, for example the ID documents in an incorporation. Download the demo files before you start:

- [demo-files.zip](/downloads/demo-files.zip) — 18 KB, SHA-256 `14c6202d666a521aafd5e632bc67fb6fc9ee23b3a5c7793fed5f507db0ff9fe1`

The package holds only made-up specimen documents, each marked SPECIMEN. It has one folder for each part of the demo, a `README.txt` and a `SHA256SUMS` file to check the files.

| Folder | Used in |
|---|---|
| `01-incorporation/` | [Incorporation](/en/demo/incorporation/#upload-the-id-documents): the ID documents of Fernreach Botanicals' two proposed directors. |
| `02-checklist/` | [Client portal](/en/demo/client-portal/#secretarial-the-checklist): the NRIC of the new director Clement Yeo, and the optional board resolution, which Rachel Lau uploads in the checklist. |
| `03-change-of-address/` | [Corporate changes](/en/demo/corporate-changes/#change-of-registered-address): the proof of Marigold Lane Kitchen's new registered office. |

The other documents of the demo, such as the case papers, the portal documents and company C's bookkeeping documents, are already in the account. You do not upload them.

{% aside type="caution" title="Upload the files exactly as they are" %}
Upload the original files from the package. Do not rename and save them again, edit them, print and scan them, or take photos of them. The demo finds the recorded answer for a document by its content: when the content changes, even slightly, there is no result for that document.
{% /aside %}

## Expiry and reset

An account can be used until its **Last day**. After that nobody can sign in to it, and it cannot be reset. Its data is kept until the platform administrator extends the account or deletes it.

The tenant admin of the account can reset it at any time: everything in the account is deleted and written again from the data pack. See [Reset and FAQ](/en/demo/reset-faq/).

